.TH AINIX 1 "October 2026" "AINIX 0.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ainix \- local NixOS assistant (help, preview, code)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ainix
[\,OPTIONS\/] [\,QUERY\/]
.SH DESCRIPTION
AINIX is a local assistant for NixOS. It answers questions from a small
knowledge base and real Nix tools, shows previews of commands, and can
generate Nix, NixOS, and flake snippets.
.PP
Preview is the default. Nothing is executed or written unless you
explicitly pass \fB--execute\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-examples
Print common usage examples.
.TP
.B \-\-list
List local knowledge topics.
.TP
.B \-\-history
Show recent queries.
.TP
.B \-\-note TEXT
Save a note that Help can search later.
.TP
.B \-\-code REQUEST
Generate a Nix, NixOS, or flake snippet. Does not write files.
.TP
.B \-\-explain
Explain a command.
.TP
.B \-\-execute, \-x
Actually run a control command. Asks for confirmation unless \fB--yes\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-yes, \-y
Skip the confirmation prompt on execute.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Simulate without running.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Print the answer only.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Less decoration.
.SH USAGE
.TP
.B ainix "How do I install a package?"
Help query. Uses local knowledge and Nix docs.
.TP
.B ainix install firefox
.TQ
.B ainix firefox
Control preview. Shows profile and declarative install lines.
.TP
.B ainix code "enable openssh"
Generate a configuration snippet.
.TP
.B ainix code "flake for myhost"
Generate a flake.nix.
.TP
.B ainix code "package mytool not in nixpkgs"
Generate a custom derivation.
.TP
.B ainix
Start interactive mode.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ainix/history.log
Query history.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ainix/notes.txt
Saved notes.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ainix/cache/
Cached Nix doc lookups.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ainix/commands.log
Log of executed commands.
.SH NOTES
AINIX does not edit your configuration files. Generated code is printed
for you to copy. Dangerous commands are blocked unless explicitly forced.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nix (1),
.BR nixos-rebuild (8),
.BR nixos-option (8)
